What is Microsoft Azure?

Microsoft Azure is a cloud computing platform that provides services such as:

Virtual Machines
Networking
Storage
Databases
Kubernetes
AI
Monitoring
Security

Instead of buying physical servers, you rent Azure resources on demand.

Azure Global Infrastructure

Microsoft operates datacenters around the world.

India
 ├── Central India
 ├── South India
 └── West India

USA
 ├── East US
 ├── East US 2
 ├── Central US
 └── West US

Europe
 ├── North Europe
 └── West Europe

A Region is one of these geographic locations where Azure hosts resources.

What is an Azure Region?

An Azure Region is a geographic area containing one or more datacenters.

Examples:

Central India
East US
West Europe
Southeast Asia
Why Regions Matter
Lower latency
Regulatory compliance
Disaster recovery
Data residency
Cost optimization
Example

If your users are mainly in Hyderabad, deploying to Central India generally provides lower latency than deploying to East US.

